## Purpose

Coordinate a recoverable Windows-native field upgrade of the exact disconnected Tool Shed instance
at `workpc:E:\dev\high_point\7520553_SMI_FW`, while routing any demonstrated installer or updater
defect back to the canonical Linux maintainer repository for the smallest reusable repair.

## Desired Outcome

The target workspace is upgraded from its observed v0.33.0 snapshot to the latest qualified stable
Tool Shed release without damaging firmware work, changing its non-Hybrid storage posture, or
leaving a target-only workaround. Recovery assets and a reusable Windows procedure remain, and any
real installer defect is repaired, cross-platform qualified, released, and proven on the target.

## Work2 Boundary

- Work2 means a committed and verified candidate plus deployment to the explicitly bound Windows
  work target, Windows-native changed-behavior checks, release-cohort registration, governed
  checkpoint, and strict health verification.
- The current repository default resolves Work2 to the combined `ts.rookaro.com` documentation
  target. That default is not applicable to this outcome and must not be invoked.
- Remote mutation begins only after an explicit verified project switch or equivalent project-bound
  target capsule for the exact Windows workspace.
- Work2 stops before pushing, tagging, or releasing a new Tool Shed version. A demonstrated defect
  that requires a new canonical release crosses into a later Work5 gate before retrying the field
  upgrade.

